
                                                    VDS BACK COMMAND


Performs Variant coding back for given infoblock.

Below is the syntax :
          vdsback 	-startaddress 0x8000 -endaddress 0x8160 -at 0x00010000 -outputfile output.bin

---------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES                   |    DESCRIPTION															    
---------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -type                   |    Type of the hex file			 										
   -name                   |    Output file name.   													
   -infoblockaddress       |    start address of the infoblock.											
   -vdslog                 |    Logging for VDS. 														
   -fillvalue              |    Values to be filled in the gaps.										
   -vctrinfoblockaddress   |    Vector infoblock address.												
---------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------


Example:
	1)	read -in input.hex vdsback -type IHEX -name medc18_output_hexmodX.hex -infoblockaddress 0x09200000 -vdslog vds.log -fillvalue 0x00
	
	2)  read -in input.hex vdsback -type IHEX -name medc18_output_hexmodX.hex -infoblockaddress 0x09200000 -vctrinfoblockaddress 0x09200000 -vdslog vds.log -fillvalue 0x00

		
